  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcome (minimum probability) and prefers the lottery with the more favorable such outcome. In this case, Lottery B has the least probable outcome (20% for 4000 Euros), which is more favorable than Lottery A's least probable outcome (25% for 3000 Euros). The individual's verbal report shows they focused on the 'higher win and lower chance', which aligns with attending to the least probable but most favorable outcomes. Furthermore, they justify their choice by minimizing the difference in probabilities, suggesting that the higher payoff under a lower probability was decisive—consistent with the logic of the decision reason. While the individual does not explicitly name the concept of 'least probable outcome', their described deliberation process matches the core logic of the reason. The emphasis on the highest gain tied to the lowest chance, and the dismissal of the small probability difference, supports the use of this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
